raspdash -- a terminal dashboard for a Raspberry Pi
===================================================

A full-screen terminal dashboard for a Raspberry Pi.  It shows:

  1. Machines   -- load, memory and temperatures of the computers on
                   the LAN
  2. Uptime     -- uptime and boots of those computers, last power cut
  3. Network    -- devices on the LAN and the services they offer
  4. Tasks      -- Google Tasks lists (read-only)
  5. Timetable  -- this week's classes from ruz.spbstu.ru
  6. Weather    -- forecasts from MET Norway for configured cities
  7-9. Markets  -- month and half-year candlestick charts (XAUT/USDT,
                   TON/USDT; BTC/USD, USD/RUB) and a comparison chart
  10. XMR       -- Monero: market, 30-day chart, network, a mining
                   calculator and your own node

Requirements
------------

A C++23 compiler (GCC 14 or later) is required, plus ncursesw, libcurl,
OpenSSL's libcrypto and nlohmann-json.

Building and installing
-----------------------

Building from a git checkout:

    ./bootstrap
    ./configure
    make
    make check

See INSTALL for generic instructions.

Enable the formatting hook once per clone:

    git config core.hooksPath hooks

Configuration
-------------

Copy config.example.toml to config.toml and edit it.  config.toml and
everything in secrets/ are personal and ignored by git.

Documentation
-------------

The Texinfo manual (doc/raspdash.texi, "info raspdash" once installed)
covers configuration and deployment on the Pi.

Reporting bugs
--------------

Report bugs to <mdddmmmm@outlook.com>, or at
https://github.com/mb6ockatf/raspdash/issues.

